# Build context of the standalone image (the root Dockerfile).
#
# An allowlist, not a list of exclusions: everything is left out, then the
# few paths the Dockerfile actually COPYs are let back in. Whatever lands in
# this folder later — a local config.yaml with broker credentials, a database,
# scratch work — stays out of the context without anyone having to think of it.
#
# The Home Assistant app is not concerned: its context is addon/zigbee-tunes/.
*

!package.json
!yarn.lock
!.yarnrc.yml
!tsconfig.json
!src/
!ui/

# Let back in with ui/, but produced on the host: a node_modules installed on
# Windows or macOS must not be copied over the one the image installs.
ui/node_modules/
ui/.yarn/
ui/dist/
ui/*.tsbuildinfo
